WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.880
Stranger Things is back with a massive slice
of 80s nostalgia and a new supernatural threat

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.460
to keep the residents of Hawkins on their
toes.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.470
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm delving into the second season

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:16.970
of Netflix's critically-acclaimed sci-fi horror
series to discuss the ending and some clues

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.020
about what it means for Season 3.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.490
I'm also starting my Stranger Things giveaway,
so, for your chance to win a Funko Pop of

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.519
your favourite Stranger Things character,
just make sure you're a subscriber and leave

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:30.349
me a comment on this video with your thoughts
about the show.

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:34.460
Spoiler alert, obviously I'm discussing the
finale of season 2 plus other episodes from

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.830
the first two seasons of Stranger Things,
so take care if you're not all caught up.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:42.899
Remember back in season 1 when Mike asked
Eleven to go to his school's annual dance,

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:43.899
the Snow Ball?

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:47.790
Well, at the end of season 2, around a year
later in the show's storyline, the pair finally

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.950
made it there!

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.289
But this is Hawkins, Indiana and, Stranger
Things is getting at least a third and fourth

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:58.090
season, so we know that things won't be "all
happily ever after" for our AV Club friends.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:02.379
And to prove just that, as the camera moves
out of the school and into its parking lot,

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:06.840
it starts to rotate, taking us back to the
Upside Down, and we see the Shadow Monster

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.420
looming over the school!

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.500
So, why is the Shadow Monster back at the
very end?

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:16.550
I mean, didn't Eleven just close the interdimensional
gateway and didn't Joyce just drive the thing

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.630
inhabiting Will's body out of him?

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.590
Well, yes, but that victory is just a temporary
one as Stranger Things creators The Duffer

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:28.460
Brothers have specifically said that the Shadow
Monster will carry over beyond season 2, becoming

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.590
a main villain of sorts for the series as
a whole.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.930
Let's look then at how our heroes defeated
the extra-dimensional big bad this season

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.751
and how their actions leave things open for
the monster's return in season 3.

00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:46.000
Similar to season 1, the Season 2 finale finds
Eleven battling the show's monster once more

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.570
to save her friends.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.930
El's role this time is to close the interdimensional
gateway, which is a cathartic experience for

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.680
her as she feels responsible for having opened
it in the first place.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:00.950
Obviously, closing the gate requires an incredible
amount of exertion on El's part.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.410
We already know that using her powers drains
her, for example, she collapsed after taking

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.350
out the agents pursuing her and her friends
at Hawkins Middle School last season.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:13.420
Thankfully, her journey away from Hawkins
to meet her mother this season also led her

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:19.030
to Kali, aka Eight, another young survivor
of Dr Brenner's experiments, and she taught

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.320
El to control her powers by channelling her
anger about events from her past.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.780
Given El's treatment at the hands of Brenner,
or Papa as she calls him, she certainly has

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.640
a lot to work with on that score.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:34.210
Still, as she tries to close the gate, you
can see the energy she summons as she even

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:38.550
levitates, and the physical toll on her is
such that she bleeds from both nostrils.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:43.360
But closing the gate isn't just about shutting
down an actual portal to the Upside Down and

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.420
saving her friends.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.130
So, what else does it mean?

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.790
Well, think back to when Kali tried to persuade
El to stay with her so they could use their

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.370
gifts against all the people who'd hurt them.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.021
In that moment, Kali used her powers on El
to make her see an apparition of Dr Brenner

00:02:58.021 --> 00:03:01.740
who told El that, 'You have to confront your
pain.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.590
You have a wound […], a terrible wound,
and it's festering, and it will grow; spread;

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.430
and eventually, it will kill you.'

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:13.350
Figuratively speaking, then, the gate El closes
is also the wound she has to repair in order

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:18.020
to heal herself of the emotional and physical
pain she endured at Hawkins Lab and of the

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:22.900
guilt she feels for unintentionally and indirectly
causing current events.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.709
And like an especially bad wound, the gate
and the surrounding area are red and angry-looking,

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:30.830
they pulsate, and something nasty seeps out.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.520
But as soon as the gate or wound is closed,
the scene is flooded with blue-tinged light,

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.790
a visual sign the characters have moved from
danger and rage to calmness and healing.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:46.270
However, that won't be the end for our chaos-causing
creature as we see the outline of the Shadow

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:51.910
Monster behind the gate before El closes it,
and that monstrous smoky tendril that reached

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:56.790
out to try and stop El from doing her job
seemed to be forced back into the Upside Down

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.270
rather than destroyed.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.730
Eleven does the heavy lifting, so to speak,
in closing the portal, but the AV Club gang

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.520
are instrumental in clearing the path for
her to reach the gate when, along with Max

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.410
and Steve, they enter the tunnels and set
the main hub area on fire, drawing the demo-dogs

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:13.430
away.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:17.320
Something interesting happens here though
when Dustin gets sprayed by a huge flower-like

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.919
creature in the tunnels.

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:22.979
He's wearing a mask at the time but complains
the spray goes in his mouth.

00:04:22.979 --> 00:04:26.580
Something similar happened to Hopper in an
earlier episode when he was sprayed and trapped

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.469
by the vines after breaking into the tunnels.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:33.289
Both Dustin and Hopper seem healthy at the
end of the season, but I wonder if there could

00:04:33.289 --> 00:04:37.749
be an incubation period for an infection that
may affect them next season.

00:04:37.749 --> 00:04:41.740
When Will was recovered from the Upside Down
in season 1, he had a huge tendril in his

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.960
mouth which presumably infected him with the
slug he coughed up later.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.060
I don't think either Dustin or Hopper will
be affected in the same way as Will, but the

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:55.099
hive-mind monster already showed how it spreads
itself and operates, and it's ominous that

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:59.439
at least two more characters have potentially
been exposed its influence.

00:04:59.439 --> 00:05:03.150
And let's not forget, there's always that
demo-dog that Dustin and Steve put into the

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.150
fridge for safe-keeping.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:09.370
Will, of course, plays a bigger role this
season than last as he becomes a host body

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.410
for the Shadow Monster at the end of the third
episode.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.729
Mike believes Will has gained the power of
truesight with the ability to see what the

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:18.370
Shadow Monster is planning.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:23.110
Mike sees this as a way for the gang to spy
on the evil entity; however, as we see later

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.840
in The Spy episode, it's the Shadow Monster
who uses Will to spy on Hawkins' residents

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.720
and manipulate events, setting a trap for
the soldiers in the tunnels.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.990
The group eventually understands that what's
inside Will is part of a hive mind, with the

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.069
Shadow Monster acting as the central brain,
which Dustin likens to the Mind Flayer in

00:05:38.069 --> 00:05:39.840
Dungeons and Dragons.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.110
Mind Flayers are evil creatures with tentacle-like
heads that feed on their victims and also

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:48.099
enslave others with telepathic mind-meld-type
powers.

00:05:48.099 --> 00:05:53.110
Mind flayers themselves are also guided by
a central elder brain, which in Stranger Things

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.220
seems to be the Shadow Monster itself.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:06:00.870
And Mind Flayers also reproduce via tadpoles
that end up implanted into humanoid beings

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:04.330
where they feed on the subject's brain and
eventually take its place.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:08.490
In Stranger Things, Will coughed up the slug-like
creature at the end of the first season and

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:13.439
the way he slowly loses his memory and identity
to the Shadow Monster in Season 2 parallels

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:18.029
the idea of Mind Flayer tadpoles slowly eating
humanoid brains.

00:06:18.029 --> 00:06:23.050
Joyce understands that this entity inside
Will is like a virus and so she sets about

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:28.180
exorcising the demon-like spirit from Will's
body by tying him up in front of a fire and

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.740
electric heaters.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.879
This works and we see the Shadow Monster leave
Will's body and escape out of the cabin into

00:06:33.879 --> 00:06:34.879
the night sky.

00:06:34.879 --> 00:06:39.259
This is a victory for Joyce in saving her
son yet again from the evil behind the Upside

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:44.610
Down, however, it hasn't necessarily been
killed, just temporarily banished and is waiting

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:45.879
to return.

